heyphony source available license, version 1.1

this is a source available licence, not an open source one. it is adapted deliberately from three
licences: the business source licence 1.1 (mariadb), which supplies the shape of a licence with a
change date and a change licence; the functional source licence 1.1 (sentry), which supplies the
permitted purposes and the competing use restriction; and the elastic licence 2.0, which supplies the
three prohibitions in section 4. it is not itself any of those licences, and it is not an spdx
identifier. sections 1 and 7 decide what it means for a particular version.

1. parameters

  licensor            tinkrland

  licensed work       the contents of the repository that carries this file, including its source
                      code, its documentation, its command line interface and any packaged or
                      bundled form of them

  additional use      none. the permitted purposes in section 2 are the whole of the grant, and
  grant               there is no further carve out hidden elsewhere in this text

  change licence      the mit licence (https://opensource.org/license/mit)

  change date         for each version, the second anniversary of the day that version was first
                      made available under this licence. section 7 records the dates

2. grant of rights

subject to sections 3, 4 and 6, the licensor grants you a non exclusive, royalty free, worldwide,
non transferable licence to use, reproduce, modify, prepare derivative works of, publicly display,
publicly perform, distribute and make the licensed work available, for a permitted purpose.

the permitted purposes are:

  - your own personal use, and the internal business use of your own organisation, including
    production use. giving an agent a phone number of its own is the intended use, not a loophole
  - evaluation, research, experimentation and prototyping
  - building applications, integrations and services that use the licensed work and are not
    themselves a competing use under section 3
  - copying and distributing the licensed work, in original or modified form, provided section 6
    is met
  - teaching, writing about, and demonstrating the licensed work

3. competing use

you may not use the licensed work, in whole or in a substantial part, to provide a commercial
product or service that substitutes for it: something a customer chooses instead of the licensed
work, in order to give a program a telephone number, an agent operated communications identity, or
a hosted inbox behind either.

three things are not a competing use, and this list is exhaustive:

  - running the licensed work for your own numbers, your own agents and your own organisation
  - charging for your own product or service where the licensed work is a supporting part of it
    rather than the thing being sold, which is to say where your value is not the number, the
    registration or the inbox
  - redistributing the licensed work unmodified and free of charge, with its licence and notices
    intact

4. three further limitations

  you may not:

  - circumvent, disable, remove or defeat any licence key, usage limit, seat limit, rate limit or
    paid feature of the licensed work, or of any service the licensor offers beside it
  - remove, obscure, or alter any notice of copyright, licence or attribution in the licensed work
  - use the licensor's names, marks, logos or product names except as required to describe the
    origin of the licensed work, or as section 6 requires

5. no trademark licence

this licence grants no rights in any trademark, service mark, trade name or logo of the licensor,
beyond the descriptive and attribution use allowed by section 4.

6. distribution

if you distribute the licensed work, or a modified version of it:

  - you must include this licence, unmodified, with the copy
  - you must keep the copyright, licence and attribution notices that the copy carries
  - you must mark modified files, and state the changes, in a way a recipient can find
  - you may not impose terms on the copy that contradict this licence, and you may not offer the
    copy under a different licence except as section 7 allows for a version whose change date has
    passed

7. change date and change licence

each version of the licensed work becomes available under the change licence on its change date,
and from that day this licence stops applying to that version. older versions convert while newer
ones stay under this licence, which is the point of dating it per version rather than per project.

  version   first made available   change date   change licence
  0.1.0     2026-11-01             2028-11-01    MIT
  0.2.0     2026-11-02             2028-11-02    MIT

a version that was never released, or a change made after a version's change date, does not inherit
that date: only a released version has one, and a release that is not listed here is dated by the
day it was first made available.

8. contributions

unless you state otherwise in writing, a contribution you submit to the licensed work is licensed to
the licensor under this licence, and you confirm you have the right to grant that.

9. termination

this licence terminates automatically if you breach it. it is reinstated, automatically and without
notice, if you cure the breach within thirty days of discovering it, or of receiving written notice
of it, whichever comes first. termination of your rights under this licence does not terminate the
rights of anyone who received the licensed work from you in compliance with it, and does not revive
any licence you had that was already terminated for breach. sections 3, 4, 5, 10 and 11 survive
termination.

10. no warranty, and the limit of liability

the licensed work is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including
without limitation any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title or non
infringement. the licensor does not warrant that the licensed work will be uninterrupted, error free,
or that any call, message or number will behave as a telephone is expected to behave.

to the maximum extent permitted by law, the licensor is not liable for any indirect, incidental,
special, consequential or punitive damages, or for any lost profits, revenue, data, goodwill or
opportunity, arising out of or related to this licence or the licensed work, whether in contract,
tort or otherwise, even if advised of the possibility. the licensor's total liability under this
licence will not exceed the greater of the amount you paid the licensor for the licensed work in the
twelve months before the claim, or one hundred united states dollars.

nothing in this licence limits liability that cannot be limited by law.

11. general

if a provision of this licence is unenforceable it is modified to the minimum extent needed to make
it enforceable, and the rest stays in force. this licence is the entire agreement between you and
the licensor about the licensed work, and it replaces anything said about it before. it is governed
by the laws applicable where the licensor is established, without regard to conflict of law rules,
and the courts of that place have exclusive jurisdiction, except that either party may seek relief
in any court of competent jurisdiction to protect its intellectual property. a waiver is only
effective in writing. if you are accepting this licence for an organisation, you confirm you are
authorised to do so on its behalf.

